issions on days 1-15). The GM accepts the decoded\n  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend\n  answer code returned for this case\".\n- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An\n  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.\n- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In a mixed\n  Mastery bundle (d15) the `NN` in each set's case ref/package names that set's SOURCE day, while the prompt text is\n  today's. Neither the case ref nor the package suffix was ever needed for the answer.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30 s (d4) and about 2.3 min\n  (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If the decoded asset already matches the answer_format, submit it.\n- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15): sets can come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.\n  A solver that branched on the day's codec name would have failed 4/5 sets. Decode each APK on its own.\n- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15): the `.so` was tiny and the answer was a literal. Use `strings`/`nm`\n  first; disassemble only if no `ANS-` literal exists.\n- **split codec order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate the candidates against the answer regex\n  instead of guessing.\n- **xor codec:** `data` is base64 first, and `key` may vary per variant (int; the solvers also accept a numeric string\n  or a repeating string key).\n- **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --\n  JSON-escaped as `<`/`>`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that\n  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`.\n- **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.\n- **6-11 s timed windows** (d2-d9) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1 s, so do no\n  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly (the solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess).\n- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove\n  server-side impact\", d13 \"app-controlled wrapping key\", d14 \"seeded nonces\", d15 \"split configuration from DEX and a\n  native library\"): judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`, cert, network config, native lib,\n  `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.\n- **Hand-typed codec tables:** use `lib.android.puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a\n  timed run.\n- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json` (no attempt_id), which makes a solved lane look\n  incomplete. Check `hctf status` before re-solving.\n- Watch for the cheap escalation (not yet seen): answer only in the dex, `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or the `.so`\n  (possibly XORed/split across `huntress_arena_secret` + a dex constant), or computed by a decrypt routine. Then trace\n  `ChallengeActivity`, run `lib.android.extract_answer`, and disassemble the exported native function.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CTNvK1L1ToAbxWHwELQNGW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LYZkTxfwY3c3JbhHUywfmp","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (30.4KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/3491ccfb-4fe4-4a96-9b27-ebe49f8ca80f/tool-results/bjujuoiwu.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D15 seen, D16+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 15 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nalways in `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native). D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. So \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\nThe risk for D16+ is the **answer leaving the puzzle JSON** (dex/arsc/.so/nested dex/encrypted) more than the theme.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3491ccfb-4fe4-4a96-9b27-ebe49f8ca80f","uuid":"d709247a-794c-4564-a5c4-f2853e3de6ef","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:16:46.358Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D15 seen, D16+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 15 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nalways in `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native). D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. So \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\nThe risk for D16+ is the **answer leaving the puzzle JSON** (dex/arsc/.so/nested dex/encrypted) more than the theme.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.x