zzle->zip->dex->apktool/jadx\n96\t   If it prints ANS-... and the prompt is the usual \"backend answer code\": submit. Do NOT chase 127.0.0.1:19090.\n97\t1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n98\t   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      puzzle codec; lib.android.puzzle_candidates / decode_any; new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n99\t   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n100\t   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n101\t   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n102\t   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n103\t   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n104\t   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n105\t   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading: unzip it, jadx it, re-run extract_answer on it\n106\t   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n107\t   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n108\t   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n109\t   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n110\t   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n111\t   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n112\t   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n113\t   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n114\t2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n115\t   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n116\t   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n117\t3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n118\t   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n119\t   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). droidasc getmanifest x.apk prints the XML.\n120\t4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n121\t   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader -> asset dex     SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher/IvParameterSpec -> static key decrypt\n122\t   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n123\t   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n124\t   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n125\t   su/magisk/RootBeer/goldfish/frida/TracerPid -> flag sits in the gated branch: read it, never run it\n126\t   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> decode names        BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n127\t   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n128\t5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n129\t   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n130\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n131\t7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n132\t8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n133\t```\n134\t\n135\t## Readiness gaps\n136\t\n137\tPriority 1 = plausible within days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n138\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change.\n139\t\n140\t```json\n141\t[\n142\t  {\"id\": \"utf16-string-pool-scan\", \"concept\": \"resources.arsc / binary AXML / meta-data hiding (rows 22, 60, 61)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n143\t   \"detail\": \"raw_entry_scan/dex_strings match ASCII bytes only; AXML (manifest) and many arsc pools are UTF-16LE, so an ANS- in strings.xml or <meta-data android:value> is missed by the fast path. Add a scan of every entry for the UTF-16LE pattern, plus androguard AXMLPrinter/ARSCParser string-pool values run through decode_any (also covers an encoded value in a res string).\"},\n144\t  {\"id\": \"nested-container-recurse\", \"concept\": \"DexClassLoader asset dex, XAPK/APKS/split, zip-in-asset (rows 42, 58)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n145\t   \"detail\": \"extract_answer stops at the outer zip. Recurse into any entry whose magic is PK\\\\x03\\\\x04 / dex\\\\n03 / XOR'd dex (try single-byte xor keys where b[:4]^k == b'dex\\\\n'): run puzzle_candidates + raw + dex_strings on the inner bytes. Cap depth 3, pure zipfile.\"},\n146\t  {\"id\": \"dex-native-split-assembly\", \"concept\": \"answer split across dex constants and .so rodata (row 38)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n147\t   \"detail\": \"D15 prompt said 'split configuration from DEX and native library' but was not split. Prebuild: collect the 'ANS-' prefix plus hex fragments (len 4-16) from the dex string pool (androguard: const-string order inside each method of ChallengeActivity/stub class) and from .so .rodata (pyelftools, ordered by address / by exported symbol), then try ordered concatenations that fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$. Prefer the order the code uses.\"},\n148\t  {\"id\": \"static-key-cipher-decode\", \"concept\": \"AES/DES with static key/IV, ECB (row 33)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n149\t   \"detail\": \"If the puzzle (or an asset) holds b64/hex ciphertext and the dex/JSON holds 16/24/32-byte strings: try AES-ECB/CBC(IV zero, IV from JSON, IV = first 16 ct bytes)/GCM/CTR and DES/3DES with every candidate key (raw, hex-decoded, b64-decoded, sha256(str)[:16|32], md5(str)), pycryptodome only; accept on ANS- regex. Bounded: 32 keys x 8 modes < 50 ms.\"},\n150\t  {\"id\": \"decode-any-chain-peel\", \"concept\": \"puzzle codec escalation (row 36)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n151\t   \"detail\": \"lib.android.decode_any's docstring cites lib.decode.peel but the code never calls it: no zlib/gzip/bz2/xz/a85/binary steps, no rot47/atbash/vigenere(str key)/rail-fence. After decode_any returns None, call lib.decode.peel(data, accept) with a deadline and add rot47/atbash/vigenere(key) to _keyed/_readings. Add regression cases for each new primitive.\"},\n152\t  {\"id\": \"native-so-emulate-export\", \"concept\": \"JNI secret computed, not a literal (rows 37, 39, 40)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n153\t   \"detail\": \"When no ANS- literal is in the .so: pyelftools to list exported funcs (Java_*, huntress_*, JNI_OnLoad) + .rodata/.data blobs; run decode_any over each blob with keys = every byte constant from capstone-disassembled 'xor reg, imm' in the export; fallback emulate a no-arg char* export with unicorn (venv-only, outside the solve.py allowlist, so worker-side helper).\"},\n154\t  {\"id\": \"dex-string-decrypt-arrays\", \"concept\": \"string-encryption helper / byte arrays in <clinit> (rows 35, 46)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n155\t   \"detail\": \"androguard: collect fill-array-data payloads and new-array const sequences plus small int/str constants in the same method; run decode_any(array, key) for each constant key. Covers xor-array obfuscation without running code.\"},\n156\t  {\"id\": \"asset-db-prefs-backup\", \"concept\": \"SQLite / SharedPreferences / .ab inside the APK (rows 16-18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n157\t   \"detail\": \"If an entry starts with 'SQLite format 3\\\\0': sqlite3.connect(':memory:').deserialize(bytes) (py3.12) and scan every text/blob cell with decode_any. shared_prefs XML: parse <string> values. 'ANDROID BACKUP' header: zlib-decompress after the header lines (unencrypted) -> tarfile -> recurse.\"},\n158\t  {\"id\": \"identity-derived-key\", \"concept\": \"predictable crypto / key from package, case ref or client_secret (rows 32, 33)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n159\t   \"detail\": \"Add keys derived from the prompt/contract and dex identity values (package suffix v<12hex>, MOB-NN-<10hex>, SECRET-..., day number) raw, as bytes and via md5/sha1/sha256 to the decode_any/cipher key list. The fixture already carries these per variant.\"},\n160\t  {\"id\": \"hermes-hbc-string-table\", \"concept\": \"React Native Hermes bundle (row 54)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n161\t   \"detail\": \"Pure-python HBC header + string table parser (small/overflow string tables, UTF-16 flag) so solve.py can scan Hermes strings with no subprocess; hermes_dec is in the venv but not on the solve.py allowlist. Worker path already works: hbc-decompiler.\"},\n162\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n163\t   \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n164\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n165\t   \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n167\t   \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"cert-and-signing-facts\", \"concept\": \"signature schemes / app links fingerprint / integrity check (rows 9, 49, 59)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n169\t   \"detail\": \"Pure python: parse META-INF/*.RSA PKCS7 (asn1 via pycryptodome or a minimal DER walk) for subject/issuer DN strings + SHA-256 cert fingerprint; scan the DN fields with decode_any. The worker path exists: apksigner verify --print-certs.\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n171\t   \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"il2cpp-metadata-literals\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n173\t   \"detail\": \"Parse global-metadata.dat header (magic 0xFAB11BAF, version) -> stringLiteral + stringLiteralData tables; scan literals. Pure python, ~60 lines. Tool alt: Il2CppDumper github release (Perfare/Il2CppDumper, net6 zip; dotnet is present).\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n175\t   \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n177\t   \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n179\t   \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n181\t   \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n182\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n183\t   \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n184\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\",\n185\t   \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"}\n186\t]\n187\t```\n188\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3491ccfb-4fe4-4a96-9b27-ebe49f8ca80f","uuid":"5b4b7caf-fd1c-4083-a9fe-2c3261617b06","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:16:50.438Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md","content":"# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D15 seen, D16+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 15 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nalways in `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native). D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. So \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\nThe risk for D16+ is the **answer leaving the puzzle JSON** (dex/arsc/.so/nested dex/encrypted) more than the theme.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.xml` | med (mixed Mastery) |\n| 5 | Custom permission weakness (normal level, typo, missing) | gap | manifest | `<permission protectionLevel=\"normal\">`, `android:permission` on comp vs `uses-permission` | `aapt dump permissions x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 6 | Task hijacking / StrandHogg | gap | manifest attrs (answer = static) | `taskAffinity`, `allowTaskReparenting=\"true\"`, `launchMode=\"singleTask\"` | `aapt dump xmltree ... \\| grep -E 'taskAffinity\\|launchMode\\|Reparent'` | med |\n| 7 | Tapjacking / overlay | gap | layout XML or manifest | `filterTouchesWhenObscured`, `FLAG_WINDOW_IS_OBSCURED`, `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | `apktool d` then `grep -r filterTouches out/res` | med |\n| 8 | Deep link (custom scheme, param parsing) | seen D2 | puzzle; real: `getQueryParameter` branch | `<data android:scheme=..>`, `getData()`, `getQueryParameter` | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme>` [i]; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 9 | App Links / autoVerify / assetlinks | gap | host + cert SHA-256 (assetlinks needs the signing fp) | `android:autoVerify=\"true\"`, `https` scheme+host | `apksigner verify --print-certs x.apk` [i]; `keytool -printcert -jarfile x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 10 | Intent redirection / nested Intent / `Intent.parseUri` | seen D3 | puzzle; real: forwarded Intent reaches a private comp | `getParcelableExtra(..Intent)`, `startActivity(`, `parseUri`, `intent://` | `jadx`; `droidasc findrefs x.apk method parseUri` | high (mixed) |\n| 11 | PendingIntent (mutable / implicit base) | seen D4 | puzzle | `FLAG_MUTABLE`, `PendingIntent.getActivity` with empty Intent | `strings -a classes.dex \\| grep -i pendingintent` | high (mixed) |\n| 12 | Fragment injection (PreferenceActivity) | gap | `isValidFragment` returns true | `PreferenceActivity`, `:android:show_fragment` | `jadx` | low |\n| 13 | WebView JS interface | seen D7 | puzzle; real: `@JavascriptInterface` getter returns secret | `addJavascriptInterface`, `@JavascriptInterface` | `jadx`; `droidasc findrefs x.apk method addJavascriptInterface` | high (mixed) |\n| 14 | WebView file access / UXSS / loadUrl from extra | gap | `assets/*.html`/`*.js` holding the secret, or the URL itself | `setAllowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs(true)`, `file:///android_asset/`, `loadUrl(getIntent()` | `unzip -l x.apk 'assets/*'`; `unzip -p x.apk 'assets/*.html'` | med-high |\n| 15 | WebView URL-allowlist bypass (`shouldOverrideUrlLoading`) | gap | allowlist check strings | `startsWith(\"https://`, `endsWith(`, `getHost()`, `loadDataWithBaseURL` | `jadx` | med |\n| 16 | allowBackup / adb backup `.ab` | seen D5 | puzzle; real: `*.ab` -> tar -> `sp/*.xml`/`db/*.db` | `allowBackup=\"true\"`, `fullBackupContent`, `dataExtractionRules`, header `ANDROID BACKUP` | `dd if=b.ab bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` [i]; abe [M] | med |\n| 17 | SharedPreferences secrets | seen D11 | puzzle; real: `shared_prefs/*.xml` or dex default value | `getSharedPreferences`, `MODE_WORLD_READABLE`, `EncryptedSharedPreferences` | `unzip -l`; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 18 | SQLite / Room / Realm | seen D12 | puzzle; real: `assets/*.db` row, `rawQuery` | `SQLiteOpenHelper`, `rawQuery`, magic `SQLite format 3\\0`, `.realm` | `sqlite3 f.db .dump` [i] | med |\n| 19 | External storage / world-readable files | gap | path constant + file in assets | `getExternalStorageDirectory`, `requestLegacyExternalStorage`, `MODE_WORLD_*` | `jadx` grep | med |\n| 20 | Logcat leakage | gap | `Log.d(tag, secret)` constant in dex | `Landroid/util/Log;`, tag strings near secret | `strings -a classes*.dex`; `jadx` grep `Log\\.` | med |\n| 21 | Clipboard / screenshot / keyboard cache | gap | n/a (fact question) | `ClipboardManager`, `FLAG_SECURE`, `textNoSuggestions` | `jadx`, `apktool d` | low-med |\n| 22 | Hardcoded secret in strings.xml / BuildConfig | gap | `resources.arsc` string, `BuildConfig` static field | `resources.arsc` present, `BuildConfig` class, `api_key`/`secret` res names | `aapt dump --values resources x.apk \\| grep -B2 ANS-` [i]; `apktool d` + `grep -r ANS- out/res`; `jadx` `BuildConfig.java` | high: cheapest escalation |\n| 23 | Firebase / google-services misconfig | gap | `firebase_database_url`, `google_api_key` res or `google-services.json` | `firebaseio.com`, `AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}`, `google_app_id` | `apktool d` + grep; offline (answer = the key/URL or a JSON in assets) | med |\n| 24 | Cloud/API keys (AWS, Stripe, JWT, OAuth) | gap | dex/arsc constants | `AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}`, `sk_live_`, `eyJ` | `strings -a` + regex; apkleaks [M] | med |\n| 25 | Cleartext traffic | seen D8 | puzzle | `usesCleartextTraffic=\"true\"`, `http://` URLs | `aapt dump xmltree` | high (mixed) |\n| 26 | Permissive TrustManager / HostnameVerifier | seen D9 | puzzle | `X509TrustManager`, empty `checkServerTrusted`, `ALLOW_ALL_HOSTNAME_VERIFIER` | `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 27 | Network Security Config | seen D10 | puzzle; NSC itself (domain/pin values) | `networkSecurityConfig`, `cleartextTrafficPermitted`, `<certificates src=\"user\">` | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml` [i] | high (mixed) |\n| 28 | Certificate pinning (OkHttp / NSC pin-set) | gap | pin `sha256/<b64>` constants; pinned host | `CertificatePinner`, `<pin-set>`, `sha256/` | `jadx`; frida [M] (no device: static only) | med-high: follows D8-D10 |\n| 29 | Bundled keystore / cert with hardcoded password | gap | `res/raw/*.bks\\|*.p12\\|*.pem`, password in dex | `KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"\\|\"PKCS12\")`, `.load(..,\"pw\".toCharArray())` | `keytool -list -v -keystore f.p12 -storepass PW` [i]; `openssl pkcs12 -in f.p12 -nodes -passin pass:PW` [i] | med |\n| 30 | Shipped traffic capture (pcap/HAR) | gap (d8 prompt hinted, none shipped) | HTTP body/header | `*.pcap`, `*.har` entries | `tshark -r f.pcap -Y http -T fields -e http.file_data` [i] | low |\n| 31 | Keystore misuse | seen D13 | puzzle | `AndroidKeyStore`, `KeyGenParameterSpec`, no `setUserAuthenticationRequired` | `jadx` | med (mixed) |\n| 32 | Predictable RNG / nonce / seed | seen D14 | puzzle; real: `new Random(seed)` -> regenerate in py | `java/util/Random`, `setSeed`, `currentTimeMillis` | `jadx`; reimplement LCG `(x*0x5DEECE66D+0xB) mod 2^48` | med (mixed) |\n| 33 | Static AES key/IV, ECB, `SecretKeySpec` | gap | ciphertext in asset/JSON + key/IV dex strings | `SecretKeySpec`, `AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding`, `IvParameterSpec`, 16/24/32-char constants | `jadx`; py `Crypto.Cipher.AES` [i] | high: the obvious \"real crypto\" codec |\n| 34 | Weak hash / KDF / short PIN | gap | hash constant -> brute force | `MessageDigest.getInstance(\"MD5\"\\|\"SHA-1\")`, `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1`, low iteration count | `jadx`; py `hashlib` brute | med |\n| 35 | String encryption helper (XOR arrays in `<clinit>`) | gap (codec xor D4/D11 is a cousin) | byte/char arrays + key in dex | `fill-array-data`, one `a(String)`/`decrypt` called everywhere | `jadx` (prints arrays); `tools/dex2jar/d2j-decrypt-string.sh` [i]; androguard | high |\n| 36 | Puzzle codec escalation (compound, zlib, rot47, vigenere) | partly seen D1-D15 | puzzle `data` with a new codec name | codec name not in `decode_payload` table | `lib.android.decode_any` (depth 3; no zlib/rot47/atbash/vigenere); `lib.decode.peel` | high: a new codec appeared D7 and D15 |\n| 37 | JNI `Java_*` / exported native secret | seen D15 | `.rodata` literal (D15) or computed in export | `lib/<abi>/*.so`, `System.loadLibrary`, `native` methods | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-`; `nm -D --defined-only f.so`; `rz-bin -zz f.so` [i] | high |\n| 38 | Answer split across dex + .so (real split) | gap (D15 prompt said split; it was not) | fragments: dex const-strings + `.so` rodata/xor | `ANS-` prefix alone, 8-hex fragments, two exports (`*_secret`, `*_day`) | `strings -a classes.dex lib/*/*.so \\| grep -E '^[0-9A-F]{4,16}$'`; `jadx` concat order | high: D15 prompt foreshadows it |\n| 39 | RegisterNatives / `JNI_OnLoad` dynamic registration | gap | fn pointer table in `.data.rel.ro` | no `Java_*` exports, `JNI_OnLoad` export, `RegisterNatives` | `rizin -A -qc 'afl; pdf @ sym.JNI_OnLoad' f.so` [i]; `analyzeHeadless` [i] | med-high |\n| 40 | Obfuscated / stripped .so (xor strings, OLLVM), multi-ABI divergence | gap | runtime-decoded stack buffer | stripped, xor loops, many `lib/<abi>/` dirs | `rizin -A`; py unicorn emulate [i]; compare `strings` per ABI | med |\n| 41 | Anti-debug (ptrace, TracerPid) | gap | flag behind the check | `ptrace`, `TracerPid`, `/proc/self/status` | `strings`; static bypass by reading the gated branch | med |\n| 42 | DexClassLoader / InMemoryDexClassLoader / asset dex | gap | `assets/*.dex\\|*.jar\\|*.apk\\|*.bin` (maybe xor/zip) | `DexClassLoader`, `InMemoryDexClassLoader`, `dex\\n03` magic inside an asset | `unzip -o -d a x.apk 'assets/*'`; `jadx -d out a/assets/payload.dex` [i] | high: classic, fits the progression |\n| 43 | Reflection / `Class.forName` obfuscation | gap | class/method names as encoded strings | `Class.forName`, `getDeclaredMethod`, `invoke` | `jadx` | med |\n| 44 | Packers (Jiagu, Bangcle, SecNeo, DexProtector) | gap | encrypted dex in assets, stub app | `libjiagu*.so`, `libsecexe.so`, `libDexHelper.so`, `StubApplication` | apkid [M]; `unzip -l` + `rz-bin -zz` | low: too heavy for a 12 KB fixture |\n| 45 | R8/ProGuard renaming | gap (fixture unobfuscated) | same places, renamed `a.b.c` | 1-2 letter class names | `jadx --deobf -d out x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 46 | DexGuard/Allatori commercial string encryption | gap | encrypted strings + decrypt stub | `o.`/`ʼ` unicode class names, huge static arrays | `jadx`; emulate the decrypt method in py | low-med |\n| 47 | Root detection (su, Magisk, RootBeer, test-keys) | gap | flag gated by `isRooted()` | `/system/xbin/su`, `RootBeer`, `test-keys`, `magisk` | `jadx`; read gated branch statically | med-high: standard MASVS-RESILIENCE theme |\n| 48 | Emulator / Frida / Xposed detection | gap | same, gated | `goldfish`, `ranchu`, `ro.kernel.qemu`, `frida`, `27042`, `XposedBridge`, `/proc/self/maps` | `strings -a`; frida [M] | med-high |\n| 49 | Signature / integrity / installer check | gap | expected cert digest constant | `GET_SIGNATURES`, `signingInfo`, `getInstallerPackageName`, `IntegrityManager` | `apksigner verify --print-certs -v x.apk` [i]; `keytool -printcert -jarfile x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 50 | Debuggable / testOnly / debug paths | gap | debug-only branch constant | `android:debuggable=\"true\"`, `testOnly`, `BuildConfig.DEBUG` | `aapt dump badging x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 51 | Smali patching / repackaging | gap | value computed at runtime (derive statically instead) | patch hint in prompt | `apktool d`, edit smali, `apktool b -o p.apk out`, `apksigner sign --ks k.jks p.apk` [i]; zipalign [M] | low: no device |\n| 52 | Flutter (Dart AOT `libapp.so`) | gap | Dart object pool strings in `libapp.so`; debug build: `flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin` | `libflutter.so`, `libapp.so`, `assets/flutter_assets/` | `strings -a lib/*/libapp.so \\| grep ANS-`; blutter [M]; reFlutter [M] | med-low |\n| 53 | React Native plain JS bundle | gap | `assets/index.android.bundle` | `libreactnativejni.so`, `__BUNDLE_START_TIME__`, `__d(function` | `webcrack` [i]; `js-beautify` [i] | med |\n| 54 | React Native Hermes bytecode | gap | HBC string table / function bodies | bundle magic `c6 1f bc 03 c1 03 19 1f`, `libhermes.so` | `hbc-decompiler b.hbc out.js` [i]; `hbc-disassembler` [i] | med |\n| 55 | Xamarin / .NET MAUI | gap | `assemblies/*.dll`, `assemblies.blob` (XALZ lz4), .NET8 `libassemblies.*.blob.so` | `libmonodroid.so`, `libxamarin-app.so`, `XALZ` / `XABA` magic | pyxamstore [M] -> `ilspycmd f.dll` [i] | low-med |\n| 56 | Unity IL2CPP / Mono | gap | `global-metadata.dat` string literals; Mono `Assembly-CSharp.dll` | `libil2cpp.so`, `libunity.so`, metadata magic `AF 1B B1 FA` | Il2CppDumper [M]; Mono: `ilspycmd` [i]; `strings` on metadata | low |\n| 57 | Cordova / Ionic / Capacitor / Kotlin MP | gap | `assets/www/*.js`, `assets/public/`, plain dex (KMP) | `cordova.js`, `capacitor.config.json`, `kotlin/` | `unzip -p` + `webcrack` [i]; `jadx` (KMP) | med (Cordova), low (KMP) |\n| 58 | Split APK / XAPK / APKS / AAB | gap | inside `base.apk` or a config split; AAB manifest is protobuf | `manifest.json` (XAPK), `toc.pb` (APKS), `BundleConfig.pb`, `base/dex/` (AAB) | `unzip -l`; bundletool [M] (`bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`) | med |\n| 59 | Signature schemes v1-v4 / cert fields | gap (v1 `META-INF/FIXTURE.RSA` every day) | signer DN fields, v2 block | `META-INF/*.RSA`, `APK Sig Block 42` | `apksigner verify -v --print-certs x.apk` [i]; `openssl pkcs7 -inform DER -in CERT.RSA -print_certs` [i] | med |\n| 60 | Manifest tricks (malformed AXML, anti-apktool, odd meta-data) | partly seen (meta-data `huntress.mechanic` daily) | `<meta-data android:value>` | apktool/jadx fail but aapt works | `aapt dump xmltree`; `apkInspector` [i]; androguard | med-high: meta-data is a natural hiding spot |\n| 61 | resources.arsc tricks (UTF-16 pools, renamed res) | gap (d10 shipped an arsc) | string resource value | arsc present; `raw_entry_scan` misses UTF-16 | `aapt dump --values resources x.apk`; `aapt2 dump resources x.apk` [i] | high |\n| 62 | ZIP-level tricks (dup entries, fake encryption bit, data after EOCD, stored polyglot) | gap | hidden entry/trailer | `unzip -l` vs `7z l` mismatch, warnings | `7z l x.apk` [i]; `apkInspector` [i]; `binwalk x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 63 | Mixed-day Mastery bundle | seen D15 | per-set puzzle (different codec per set) | `day` field / `DAY-NN` tag differ per set | `puzzle_candidates` per APK, never branch on today | high |\n| 64 | iOS IPA (if the lane ever goes iOS) | gap | `Info.plist`, Mach-O `__cstring`, embedded plist/json | `Payload/*.app/`, Mach-O `cffaedfe`, `CFBundleIdentifier` | py `plistlib` [i]; `rz-bin -zz Payload/X.app/X` [i]; lief [i]; ipsw/class-dump [M] | low |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"   # puzzle->zip->dex->apktool/jadx\n   If it prints ANS-... and the prompt is the usual \"backend answer code\": submit. Do NOT chase 127.0.0.1:19090.\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      puzzle codec; lib.android.puzzle_candidates / decode_any; new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading: unzip it, jadx it, re-run extract_answer on it\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). droidasc getmanifest x.apk prints the XML.\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader -> asset dex     SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher/IvParameterSpec -> static key decrypt\n   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n   su/magisk/RootBeer/goldfish/frida/TracerPid -> flag sits in the gated branch: read it, never run it\n   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> decode names        BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"utf16-string-pool-scan\", \"concept\": \"resources.arsc / binary AXML / meta-data hiding (rows 22, 60, 61)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"raw_entry_scan/dex_strings match ASCII bytes only; AXML (manifest) and many arsc pools are UTF-16LE, so an ANS- in strings.xml or <meta-data android:value> is missed by the fast path. Add a scan of every entry for the UTF-16LE pattern, plus androguard AXMLPrinter/ARSCParser string-pool values run through decode_any (also covers an encoded value in a res string).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nested-container-recurse\", \"concept\": \"DexClassLoader asset dex, XAPK/APKS/split, zip-in-asset (rows 42, 58)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"extract_answer stops at the outer zip. Recurse into any entry whose magic is PK\\\\x03\\\\x04 / dex\\\\n03 / XOR'd dex (try single-byte xor keys where b[:4]^k == b'dex\\\\n'): run puzzle_candidates + raw + dex_strings on the inner bytes. Cap depth 3, pure zipfile.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-native-split-assembly\", \"concept\": \"answer split across dex constants and .so rodata (row 38)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D15 prompt said 'split configuration from DEX and native library' but was not split. Prebuild: collect the 'ANS-' prefix plus hex fragments (len 4-16) from the dex string pool (androguard: const-string order inside each method of ChallengeActivity/stub class) and from .so .rodata (pyelftools, ordered by address / by exported symbol), then try ordered concatenations that fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$. Prefer the order the code uses.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"static-key-cipher-decode\", \"concept\": \"AES/DES with static key/IV, ECB (row 33)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"If the puzzle (or an asset) holds b64/hex ciphertext and the dex/JSON holds 16/24/32-byte strings: try AES-ECB/CBC(IV zero, IV from JSON, IV = first 16 ct bytes)/GCM/CTR and DES/3DES with every candidate key (raw, hex-decoded, b64-decoded, sha256(str)[:16|32], md5(str)), pycryptodome only; accept on ANS- regex. Bounded: 32 keys x 8 modes < 50 ms.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"decode-any-chain-peel\", \"concept\": \"puzzle codec escalation (row 36)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"lib.android.decode_any's docstring cites lib.decode.peel but the code never calls it: no zlib/gzip/bz2/xz/a85/binary steps, no rot47/atbash/vigenere(str key)/rail-fence. After decode_any returns None, call lib.decode.peel(data, accept) with a deadline and add rot47/atbash/vigenere(key) to _keyed/_readings. Add regression cases for each new primitive.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-so-emulate-export\", \"concept\": \"JNI secret computed, not a literal (rows 37, 39, 40)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"When no ANS- literal is in the .so: pyelftools to list exported funcs (Java_*, huntress_*, JNI_OnLoad) + .rodata/.data blobs; run decode_any over each blob with keys = every byte constant from capstone-disassembled 'xor reg, imm' in the export; fallback emulate a no-arg char* export with unicorn (venv-only, outside the solve.py allowlist, so worker-side helper).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-string-decrypt-arrays\", \"concept\": \"string-encryption helper / byte arrays in <clinit> (rows 35, 46)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"androguard: collect fill-array-data payloads and new-array const sequences plus small int/str constants in the same method; run decode_any(array, key) for each constant key. Covers xor-array obfuscation without running code.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"asset-db-prefs-backup\", \"concept\": \"SQLite / SharedPreferences / .ab inside the APK (rows 16-18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"If an entry starts with 'SQLite format 3\\\\0': sqlite3.connect(':memory:').deserialize(bytes) (py3.12) and scan every text/blob cell with decode_any. shared_prefs XML: parse <string> values. 'ANDROID BACKUP' header: zlib-decompress after the header lines (unencrypted) -> tarfile -> recurse.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"identity-derived-key\", \"concept\": \"predictable crypto / key from package, case ref or client_secret (rows 32, 33)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"Add keys derived from the prompt/contract and dex identity values (package suffix v<12hex>, MOB-NN-<10hex>, SECRET-..., day number) raw, as bytes and via md5/sha1/sha256 to the decode_any/cipher key list. The fixture already carries these per variant.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"hermes-hbc-string-table\", \"concept\": \"React Native Hermes bundle (row 54)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"Pure-python HBC header + string table parser (small/overflow string tables, UTF-16 flag) so solve.py can scan Hermes strings with no subprocess; hermes_dec is in the venv but not on the solve.py allowlist. Worker path already works: hbc-decompiler.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cert-and-signing-facts\", \"concept\": \"signature schemes / app links fingerprint / integrity check (rows 9, 49, 59)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"Pure python: parse META-INF/*.RSA PKCS7 (asn1 via pycryptodome or a minimal DER walk) for subject/issuer DN strings + SHA-256 cert fingerprint; scan the DN fields with decode_any. The worker path exists: apksigner verify --print-certs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n   \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cpp-metadata-literals\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"Parse global-metadata.dat header (magic 0xFAB11BAF, version) -> stringLiteral + stringLiteralData tables; scan literals. Pure python, ~60 lines. Tool alt: Il2CppDumper github release (Perfare/Il2CppDumper, net6 zip; dotnet is present).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n   \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\",\n   \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":188,"startLine":1,"totalLines":188}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019YarybEQA72duqxF61KPHU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
