{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5yojdDU7GGtUp9bs2SV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G8s8QgfK1W7bjpsvCR3136","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='reference/techniques/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-15; updated after every day)\",\"# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-16; updated after every day)\")\nrep(\"\"\"`resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, 12772 B). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16\n  uppercase hex.\"\"\",\"\"\"`resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, ~12.8 KB). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` +\n  16 uppercase hex.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` \"challenge-owned JNI shared library\" d15). The theme was flavour only: no day\n  required exploiting it, even with a matching stub class (`WebViewBridge`, `CleartextSession`, `TrustEveryone`,\n  `PredictableCrypto`, `NativeLibrarySecrets`) or a prompt demanding a live action.\"\"\",\"\"\"  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` \"challenge-owned JNI shared library\" d15, `jni_length` \"Java-to-native validation\n  mismatch\" d16). The theme was flavour only: no day required exploiting it, even with a matching stub class\n  (`WebViewBridge`, `TrustEveryone`, `PredictableCrypto`, `NativeLibrarySecrets`, `JNIBoundary`) or a prompt demanding a\n  live action. d16 is the first day whose TT/Mastery build had a REAL gate in code (a JNI export guarding the answer),\n  yet the answer was still a literal in the asset and in `.rodata`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  caesar+key, then repeats; d15 a NEW name `native` whose `data` is already the plaintext answer).\"\"\",\"\"\"  caesar+key, then repeats; d15-d16 `native`, whose `data` is already the plaintext answer).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **d15: Mastery became a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets were APKs from earlier days (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d10 split,\n  d14 caesar, d15 native in one attempt; MOB-03/07/09/13/15 in another contract), all under today's prompt text. Up to\n  d14 every set used the day's codec. Solve each set from its own puzzle JSON, never from \"today's codec\".\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Since d15 Mastery is a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets are APKs from earlier days plus one of today's (d15: d01 plain,\n  d07 caesar, d10 split, d14 caesar, d15 native; d16: d01 plain, d04 xor, d11 xor, d13 base64, d16 native), all under\n  today's prompt text. Solve each set from its own puzzle JSON, never from \"today's codec\".\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 15 days.\"\"\",\"\"\"accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 16 days.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Escalation watch: d15 shipped the first native lib, but the answer was STILL in the asset as well (and as a plain\n  `.rodata` string in the `.so`). If a later day drops it from the asset, the `.so`/dex are the next places\n  (`lib.android.extract_answer` has the zip/dex/apktool fallback chain).\"\"\",\"\"\"- Escalation watch: d15 shipped the first native lib and d16 the first native GATE (`Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence\n  (env, cls, int len)` returns `arena_value` only if `huntress_arena_length_accepts(len, 0)`: `len > 0xffff &&\n  (uint16)len == 0`, i.e. 65536). The answer was STILL in the asset and in `.rodata`. If a later day drops it from the\n  asset, read the gate statically and take the value it returns (`lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain).\"\"\")\n# variant axes\nrep(\"\"\"- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44; caesar shift\n  d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9/10/17,4,7, d15 Mastery d07-set 15, d14-set 4)\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44, d16 Mastery\n  d04-set 21, d11-set 232; caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9/10/17,4,7, d15 Mastery d07-set 15, d14-set 4)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  source day). The day picks re-roll per attempt (01/07/10/14/15 vs 03/07/09/13/15); the last set was today's.\n  Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding (`puzzle_candidates` over each APK) -- never branch on the challenge's day.\"\"\",\"\"\"  source day). The day picks re-roll per attempt (d15: 01/07/10/14/15 vs 03/07/09/13/15; d16: 01/04/11/13/16); the last\n  set was today's. d16: the QUESTION's case ref/package (`MOB-06-..`, `d08`, `d14`) did NOT match the APK's own\n  (`MOB-04`, `d11`, `d13`), so the contract text does not predict the codec either.\n  Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding (`puzzle_candidates` over each APK) -- never branch on the day or case ref.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. Set count varies: 3 sets\n  (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets (d8, d9, d15).\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. Set count varies: 3 sets\n  (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets (d8, d9, d15, d16).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON (d15: also duplicated in the `.so`); if it decodes to nothing,\n  fall back to dex/resources/native (`raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`).\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON (d15-d16: also duplicated in the `.so` `.rodata`); if it decodes\n  to nothing, fall back to dex/resources/native (`raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`).\n- **Native lib shape (NEW d16)** -- same day, different `.so` builds: the single variant shipped the d15-style 13648 B lib\n  (exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day` only, dex 2584 B, no `loadLibrary`); TT and the Mastery d16 set\n  shipped a 14128 B lib adding 