hind `ptrace`/`/proc/self/status`/`su` checks in a native export | imports `ptrace`, `fopen`, `access`, strings `TracerPid`, `/system/bin/su`, `frida` | `rz-bin -i f.so`; `objdump -d`; read the passing branch statically | med-high: native track continues |\n| 64 | iOS IPA\"\"\")\n# cues\nrep(\"\"\"   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\"\"\",\"\"\"   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    Java_*_native*(int) + *_accepts helper (D16 gate): objdump -d it; the value it returns\n                                    is the answer (D16: &arena_value = the .rodata ANS- literal; bypass len 65536)\"\"\")\n# gaps json\ni=s.index(\"```json\\n\")+len(\"```json\\n\"); j=s.index(\"```\",i)\ngaps=json.loads(s[i:j])\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndef built(g): \n    v=st.get('mobile-android:'+g['id'])\n    return v and (v.get('ok') or v.get('attempts',0)>=2)\nkeep=[g for g in gaps if not (g['action']=='prebuild' and built(g))]\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"jni-export-return-trace\",\"concept\":\"answer returned only through a gated/computed JNI export (rows 37, 65)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D16 TT returned &arena_value from Java_*_nativeEvidence behind a length gate. Pure python (pyelftools + capstone): for every Java_* / huntress_* export, disassemble to ret, collect rip-relative lea/mov targets (x86_64) and adrp+add pairs (arm64), read the C string / bytes at each target in .rodata/.data, and run ANS regex + decode_any on them (with xor keys = imm bytes seen in the function). Return the candidate the export can return. Catches the day the literal leaves the asset.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jni-gate-bypass-input\",\"concept\":\"JNI type/length narrowing gate: which input passes (row 65)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"If a question asks for the bypass value/type (not just ANS-): for a small checker export (< 0x100 bytes, int args), emulate it with unicorn over boundary inputs {0,1,0x7f,0x80,0xff,0x100,0x7fff,0x8000,0xffff,0x10000,0x10001,0x7fffffff,-1,-0x8000,-0x10000} and second-arg combos from the caller's immediates; report the smallest passing input and the narrowing (u8/u16/s16/u32). Worker-side helper (unicorn outside the solve.py allowlist) plus a capstone-only pattern matcher (cmp $0xffff + 16-bit cmp) for solve.py.\"},\n {\"id\":\"registernatives-table\",\"concept\":\"JNI_OnLoad / RegisterNatives dynamic registration (row 39)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"No Java_* exports but JNI_OnLoad present: pyelftools walk .data.rel.ro/.data with R_*_RELATIVE relocations to find JNINativeMethod {char* name, char* sig, void* fn} triples whose name matches a dex `native` method name; map each to its fn address and feed jni-export-return-trace. Pure python, x86_64 + arm64.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-stack-string\",\"concept\":\"answer assembled on the stack in a native export (row 40)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"capstone scan of each exported function for runs of `mov byte/dword/qword [rbp/rsp - off], imm` (x86_64) and `mov w/x, #imm; strb/str` (arm64); order bytes by stack offset, then ANS regex + decode_any (xor with every imm8 in the function, add/sub per-index). Common 'native secret' obfuscation that defeats strings.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-abi-arm-native\",\"concept\":\"multi-ABI libs / arm64-only .so (row 40)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"So far only lib/x86_64. Make every native extractor ABI-aware: iterate lib/*/ (arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a thumb, x86, x86_64), pick capstone arch/mode from e_machine + EI_CLASS, compare candidates across ABIs and prefer one confirmed by >=2 ABIs or by the asset. Add a regression case per ABI built with the local toolchain if available.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-native-call-args\",\"concept\":\"Java side of the JNI boundary: native method sigs and call-site constants (row 65)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"androguard: list `native` methods (name, descriptor I/J/S/[B/String) and, for each invoke of them, the const/const-wide/const-string values loaded into the argument registers in the caller (plus String.length()/getBytes().length checks before the call). Output facts for questions like 'which length/type crosses the boundary' and feed the args to jni-gate-bypass-input.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-gated-branch-read\",\"concept\":\"native anti-debug / root / emulator gate (rows 41, 47, 48, 66)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"capstone: in each export find calls to ptrace/fopen/access/strstr (via PLT/GOT names from pyelftools) and the conditional branch on their result; collect data refs reachable on BOTH sides of the branch and run ANS regex + decode_any. Static only, never execute; returns the value on the 'not debugged / not rooted' path.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-gated-branch-consts\",\"concept\":\"root / emulator / signature check in Java gating a constant (rows 47-49)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"androguard: methods referencing su/magisk/test-keys/goldfish/ranchu/frida/TracerPid/GET_SIGNATURES strings; collect const-string / array payloads in the same method and its callers, run decode_any with keys from small int consts. Answer sits in the gated branch.\"},\n {\"id\":\"webview-asset-js-scan\",\"concept\":\"WebView assets html/js holding or decoding the answer (rows 13, 14, 57)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"For assets/**/*.html|*.js|*.json (incl. assets/www, flutter_assets): extract JS string literals, atob(...) args, String.fromCharCode lists, \\\\x/\\\\u escapes and hex arrays; run decode_any over each and over simple XOR-with-literal-key pairs found in the same file. Pure stdlib regex, no JS engine.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cert-pin-and-nsc-facts\",\"concept\":\"certificate pinning pins / NSC pin-set (rows 27, 28)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Collect `sha256/<b64>` pins from the dex string pool and <pin-set><pin digest> from res/xml/*.xml (AXML via androguard), plus pinned hostnames; expose as facts and as decode_any inputs (b64 -> hex). Covers a fact question ('which pin/host') and an answer encoded as a pin.\"}\n]\nids={g['id'] for g in gaps}\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids\nallg=new+keep\nallg.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nout=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in allg)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(out)\ns=s[:i]+out+s[j:]\nrep(\"\"\"Priority 1 = plausible within days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change.\"\"\",\"\"\"Priority 1 = plausible within days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\nutf16-string-pool-scan, nested-container-recurse, dex-native-split-assembly, static-key-cipher-decode,\ndecode-any-chain-peel, native-so-emulate-export, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, asset-db-prefs-backup, identity-derived-key,\nhermes-hbc-string-table, cert-and-signing-facts, il2cpp-metadata-literals.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ni=s.index(\"```json\\n\")+8; j=s.index(\"```\",i); g=json.loads(s[i:j])\nprint(len(g), sum(1 for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild'), [x['id'] for x in g])\na=s.index(\"## Recognition cues\"); b=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); print('cue lines', s[a:b].count('\\n'))\nEOF\nwc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"}}}
